Check Ubuntu Firewall
Run:



sudo ufw status
If Active, run:



sudo ufw allow 8080/tcp
sudo ufw reload
Check Azure Networking
Azure Portal:



Ubuntu1
→ Networking
Look under Inbound port rules.

You must see something like:



Priority : 100
Source   : Any
Protocol : TCP
Port     : 8080
Action   : Allow
If you don't see 8080:

Click Add inbound port rule
Fill:


Source              : Any
Source port ranges  : *
Destination         : Any
Service             : Custom
Destination Port    : 8080
Protocol            : TCP
Action              : Allow
Priority            : 100
Name                : Allow-8080
Click Add
Wait 1-2 minutes.

Verify Public IP
Run:



curl ifconfig.me
or check:



VM → Overview → Public IP Address
Use:



http://20.81.45.96:8080
Quick Test
From your PC:



telnet 20.81.45.96 8080
or PowerShell:



Test-NetConnection 20.81.45.96 -Port 8080
If it says:



TcpTestSucceeded : False
then Azure NSG is still blocking the port.

Please send a screenshot of:



Azure Portal
→ Ubuntu1
→ Networking
→ Inbound port rules
That screen will immediately show why port 8080 is inaccessible.





