UBUNTU VM TO ADD IN DEPLOYMENT GROUP STEPS
Copilot said:
To add an Ubuntu VM to an Azure DevOps Deployment Group, follow these steps.

Step 1: Create Deployment Group
In Azure DevOps:



Pipelines
→ Deployment groups
→ New
Enter:



Deployment Group Name : Ubuntu-Tomcat-DG
Description           : Ubuntu Tomcat Server
Click:



Create
Azure DevOps will show a Linux registration script.

Step 2: Create PAT Token
Azure DevOps:



Top Right Profile
→ Personal Access Tokens
→ New Token
Select:



Scopes:
Deployment Groups (Read, Manage)
Agent Pools (Read, Manage)
Create and copy the PAT token.

Step 3: Connect to Ubuntu VM
SSH to VM:



ssh azureuser@20.81.45.96
Become root:



sudo su -
Step 4: Install Deployment Group Agent
Create folder:



mkdir /azagent
cd /azagent
Download agent (check latest version in Azure DevOps page, example below):



wget https://vstsagentpackage.azureedge.net/agent/4.263.0/vsts-agent-linux-x64-4.263.0.tar.gz
Extract:

curl -L -o agent.tar.gz https://download.agent.dev.azure.com/agent/4.263.0/vsts-agent-linux-x64-4.263.0.tar.gz

tar zxvf vsts-agent-linux-x64-4.263.0.tar.gz
Step 5: Configure Agent
Run:



./config.sh
Provide:



Server URL:
https://dev.azure.com/<your-org>
 
Authentication Type:
PAT
 
PAT:
<Paste Token>
 
Deployment Group:
Ubuntu-Tomcat-DG
 
Agent Name:
Tomcat-Ubuntu-Agent
Select:



Y
when asked to configure as deployment group agent.

Step 6: Install Service


sudo ./svc.sh install
sudo ./svc.sh start
Check status:



sudo ./svc.sh status
Expected:



Service is running
Step 7: Verify in Azure DevOps
Go to:



Pipelines
→ Deployment Groups
→ Ubuntu-Tomcat-DG
You should see:



Tomcat-Ubuntu-Agent
Online
Healthy
Step 8: Create Release Pipeline
Add stage:



Deploy to Ubuntu
Select Deployment Group:



Ubuntu-Tomcat-DG
Step 9: Deploy WAR to Tomcat
Add Bash task:



sudo cp $(System.DefaultWorkingDirectory)/**/*.war /var/lib/tomcat10/webapps/
 
sudo systemctl restart tomcat10
Or if your path is:



/opt/tomcat/webapps
then use:



sudo cp $(System.DefaultWorkingDirectory)/**/*.war /opt/tomcat/webapps/
 
sudo systemctl restart tomcat10
